+The root entrypoint exposes providers/global feedback; focused `@planicam/shared/ui/<control>` entrypoints expose controls through their component index. Use explicit named exports; do not export raw PrimeNG or PrimeIcons symbols.
 
 ## Logo
 
@@ -35,3 +35,11 @@ Before changing PrimeNG controls, read [`primeng-llms.txt`](../../../docs/develo
 ## Validation
 
 Run `bun nx lint shared-ui`.
+
+## Workspace controls and overlays
+
+`Dialog` delegates focus trapping, modal masking, Escape and overflow to PrimeNG; feature-owned busy state prevents user dismissal during persistence. Programmatic close always hides after an owner handles a successful operation, even before the next bound busy input update. `cancelled` is a cancellable output, while showModal/close support existing feature commands. `Popover` anchors to its trigger or an explicitly supplied event and restores focus through PrimeNG. `Confirmations.confirm(message,event?,dialog?)` resolves a boolean; default anchored ConfirmPopup is for destructive actions, with escape/outside/reject resolving false. The explicit dialog variant is reserved for contextual batch assignment. The application renders one ConfirmationHost. Overlays carry no domain persistence.
+
+`Select` binds a Signal Forms field directly or uses value/valueChange for controlled presentation. `OptionsControl` is a domain-neutral technical mapping for text, textarea, number, select, multiSelect, selectButton, checkbox, switch and date. It binds internal Signal Forms to native PrimeNG controls and emits unchanged primitive values; numeric zero and required false are retained. Report schema/required/readiness rules remain outside shared-ui. Choice values are strings or finite numeric primitives. Dates emit ISO calendar dates from calendar selection or keyboard blur; invalid typed dates emit null for owning-schema validation. Numeric controls forward input and committed blur values. Status, CountBadge, InlineMessage, Progress and DividerLine wrap Tag, Badge, Message, ProgressBar and Divider; they do not own report semantics.
+
+Accordion, Tree, DataTable and Stepper retain PrimeNG interaction. Tree accepts hierarchy and a row template; DataTable supports explicit multi-selection/header templates; Stepper exposes an owning-workflow maxStep. Keyboard names, errors and hints belong on actual control inputs. Vendor imports stay inside shared-ui. The installed PrimeNG 22 type/source metadata was the fallback during initial wrapper implementation while the PrimeNG MCP was unavailable. After it became available, the corrected Popover wrapper passed generated API metadata validation; that check is separate from Angular build and browser interaction evidence.

